-- Task set-witness-discrete-float-strict-comparison-at-atom: a strict
-- comparison of a discrete Float draw at one of its atoms. v is 2.0 or 1.0
-- with mass 0.5 each, so v < 2.0 holds exactly at v = 1.0. Once the let is
-- not densely enumerated (--materializationBudget 0, the corpus's
-- BudgetZeroMatchesDefault sweep) the set-witness engine took the continuous
-- reading: v < 2.0 as [-inf, 2.0] and its negation as [2.0, inf] measured as
-- CDF(inf) - CDF(2.0), which counted the atom at 2.0 on the True side and
-- dropped it from the False side (p(Left ()) = 0.0, p(Right 2.0) = 0.5).
main = draw v = (if Uniform < 0.5 then 2.0 else 1.0) in if v < 2.0 then right v else left ()
